wine-sg (10.0-1111) unstable; urgency=medium

  * 9200 ntdll: a process whose new wineserver dies before answering it
    ends with an error; it waited for ever. The process kept its own copy
    of its reply pipe's write end until the server's reply came, so a
    server killed or crashed in that moment ("wineserver -k" while a
    session starts, bugs1 2026-11-22) left it blocked in read() with its
    parent waiting on it. The copy is now closed once it is sent (the
    server has its own), so a dead server means end-of-file, and while a
    process is being started that is "wine: the wineserver exited before
    it finished starting this process" with status 1. Gate test-srvdeath
    (a stand-in server that dies after taking the first request), mutant
    SG_MUTANT_KEEP_REPLY_WRITER.

