    about a second after it changes, as Windows' lazy writer does, and at a
    normal exit, not only when its handle is closed. Visual Studio's private
    registry was never saved, so its first-launch window came back on every
    start and VsRegEdit's settings were lost. test-apphive.

 -- Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>  Mon, 16 Nov 2026 12:29:41 -0800

wine-sg (10.0-923) unstable; urgency=medium

  * 7807 shell32: a move to the Recycle Bin from the profile is a rename.
    The profile is a bind mount of the home and the Trash is reached through
    /home, so a delete copied the whole file (15 GB, a minute at "100%",
    Cancel ignored). The Trash is now found through the file's own mount;
    Restore too. A move that has to copy (another disk) shows its bytes and
    stops at Cancel; an item counts when it is gone. The Recycle Bin menu
    takes "undelete"/"delete" by name. test-trashmount.

 -- Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>  Mon, 16 Nov 2026 12:26:23 -0800

